mothershipOS (mship.audio): the primary module has the phone's audio devices, each its own ALSA
PCM of the guest's virtio-snd card (0 speaker, 1 earpiece, 2 wired headset/headphones, 3 built-in
mic, 4 back mic, 5 wired headset mic), so Android's audio policy routes between them natively.
Earpiece and back mic are attached devices; wired headset, headphones and headset mic are analog
template ports the framework connects on jack events (ModulePrimary accepts analog connections).
StreamPrimary picks the PCM by device type when the address has no CARD_x_DEV_y; a card without
that PCM (stock Cuttlefish) keeps using the default one. A running stream moves to the new device's
PCM at once when the routing changes (stock: only at the next start, after a standby, so media kept
playing on the headset after "Phone speaker" was picked).

